[
  "For a while,",
  "the front doors",
  "of Galveston opened",
  "onto empty air.",
  "Beneath the houses stood",
  "forests of wooden supports.",
  "Above the muddy ground,",
  "narrow walkways led",
  "people home.",
  "This was",
  "not the storm itself.",
  "This was the rebuilding.",
  "And it began",
  "with an extraordinary question:",
  "how do you save",
  "a city",
  "when the ground",
  "beneath it",
  "is too low?",
  "At the turn",
  "of the twentieth century,",
  "Galveston was one",
  "of the busiest ports",
  "in the American South.",
  "Cotton moved",
  "through its docks.",
  "Trains brought goods",
  "and visitors.",
  "Ships connected Texas",
  "to the wider world.",
  "But Galveston had",
  "a weakness",
  "that could",
  "not be seen",
  "on a ledger.",
  "The city stood",
  "on a long,",
  "low barrier island",
  "off the Texas coast.",
  "The highest natural ground",
  "on the island",
  "was estimated",
  "to be less",
  "than nine feet",
  "above sea level.",
  "The sea was part",
  "of its prosperity,",
  "but it was also",
  "close enough",
  "to become a threat.",
  "In June 1900,",
  "the census counted",
  "almost thirty-eight thousand people",
  "in the city.",
  "Families lived",
  "in wooden houses.",
  "Children walked to school.",
  "Shopkeepers opened their doors.",
  "For most of them,",
  "September 8 began like",
  "another day",
  "on the Gulf Coast.",
  "Days earlier,",
  "a tropical storm",
  "had crossed Cuba.",
  "It strengthened",
  "as it moved",
  "across the Gulf.",
  "At the time, there",
  "were no weather satellites,",
  "no radar maps",
  "on a phone,",
  "and no way",
  "for forecasters to follow",
  "a hurricane",
  "over open water",
  "with anything",
  "like modern precision.",
  "Reports came",
  "from scattered observations, ships,",
  "and telegraph stations.",
  "A storm warning flag",
  "was raised in Galveston",
  "on September 7.",
  "The danger",
  "was not entirely unknown.",
  "But many residents",
  "did not expect",
  "the catastrophe",
  "that was approaching.",
  "Some had experienced",
  "earlier storms",
  "and believed their city",
  "could withstand another.",
  "Isaac Cline,",
  "the local",
  "Weather Bureau official,",
  "watched conditions change.",
  "The next day",
  "the sea was rising,",
  "the wind was strengthening,",
  "and the information reaching",
  "the public",
  "could not show",
  "the full scale",
  "of what was coming.",
  "On the morning",
  "of September 8,",
  "water began",
  "creeping into the streets.",
  "Then the Gulf",
  "pushed farther inland.",
  "By afternoon,",
  "people who had expected",
  "bad weather",
  "were confronting something",
  "far worse.",
  "The water",
  "was not simply rain",
  "collecting in low places.",
  "The hurricane",
  "drove a massive surge",
  "across the island.",
  "The storm surge",
  "was later",
  "estimated at nearly",
  "sixteen feet.",
  "Waves carried timbers,",
  "pieces of houses,",
  "and everything else",
  "they could tear loose.",
  "As debris struck buildings,",
  "some walls gave way.",
  "Other structures were lifted",
  "from their foundations.",
  "People climbed",
  "to upper floors",
  "and gathered",
  "in stronger buildings.",
  "Families took in neighbors.",
  "One building that survived",
  "was the Gresham family's",
  "stone house,",
  "known today",
  "as Bishop's Palace.",
  "According to accounts",
  "of survivors,",
  "more than two hundred",
  "residents found refuge there.",
  "Yet height offered little",
  "certainty as water",
  "and wreckage",
  "moved through the city.",
  "At the Weather Bureau,",
  "the wind gauge",
  "recorded gusts",
  "of roughly",
  "one hundred miles",
  "an hour",
  "before it blew away.",
  "Conditions grew",
  "more violent",
  "into the evening.",
  "Darkness made",
  "it harder to see",
  "where the water ended",
  "or what was coming",
  "toward a house.",
  "Cline and his family",
  "struggled to survive.",
  "His wife",
  "died in the storm.",
  "Their loss",
  "was one among",
  "thousands across Galveston,",
  "and many families",
  "would never",
  "be whole again.",
  "Near midnight,",
  "the wind and water",
  "finally began to subside.",
  "What daylight revealed",
  "was a city transformed.",
  "Streets were buried",
  "beneath wreckage.",
  "Houses had disappeared",
  "or been torn apart.",
  "Survivors searched for relatives",
  "among unfamiliar piles",
  "of broken timber.",
  "The death toll",
  "could never be counted",
  "with complete certainty.",
  "At least",
  "six thousand people died.",
  "Some estimates",
  "are considerably higher,",
  "and the storm remains",
  "the deadliest",
  "weather-related natural disaster",
  "in United States history.",
  "The city faced",
  "an immediate task",
  "as terrible",
  "as the storm itself:",
  "caring for the living",
  "and finding the dead.",
  "Temporary morgues were established.",
  "As the scale",
  "of the losses became",
  "clear, recovery workers struggled",
  "with more bodies than",
  "the city could handle.",
  "Aid came from outside,",
  "but the future",
  "was uncertain.",
  "Galveston could rebuild",
  "its homes and businesses.",
  "Yet if another",
  "hurricane drove",
  "water over the island,",
  "the same low ground",
  "would be waiting",
  "beneath them.",
  "Rebuilding also",
  "meant living with uncertainty.",
  "A replacement house",
  "could be swept away",
  "by a future surge.",
  "Businesses needed",
  "a functioning port,",
  "families needed homes,",
  "and the island needed",
  "a way",
  "to face the water",
  "that surrounded it.",
  "The question",
  "was no longer",
  "simply how to restore",
  "the city.",
  "It was",
  "how to give it",
  "a better chance",
  "next time.",
  "A board of engineers",
  "proposed two connected defenses.",
  "First came a seawall",
  "along the Gulf side:",
  "a massive barrier",
  "designed to meet",
  "the waves",
  "before they reached",
  "the streets.",
  "But a wall",
  "alone would leave",
  "a problem behind it.",
  "Much of the city",
  "still lay",
  "close to sea level.",
  "The second",
  "part of the plan",
  "was almost",
  "harder to imagine.",
  "They would raise",
  "the ground.",
  "And before the ground",
  "could rise, buildings",
  "standing on it",
  "would have to rise",
  "too.",
  "Work on the first",
  "section of the seawall",
  "began in 1902.",
  "By 1904,",
  "a concrete barrier",
  "about three point three",
  "miles long",
  "stood along the Gulf.",
  "Its top rose",
  "seventeen feet",
  "above mean low water.",
  "Later extensions would carry",
  "the wall farther",
  "along the coast.",
  "While the seawall",
  "was being built,",
  "the grade-raising project turned",
  "neighborhoods",
  "into construction sites",
  "behind it.",
  "The work moved",
  "from section to section.",
  "Crews lifted",
  "buildings",
  "on hand-operated screw jacks",
  "and supported",
  "them on temporary timbers.",
  "About two thousand",
  "buildings were raised,",
  "according to the American",
  "Society of Civil Engineers.",
  "That number tells only",
  "part of the story.",
  "A building",
  "could not simply",
  "be set aside",
  "while a new foundation",
  "was prepared.",
  "It had to remain",
  "supported as crews worked",
  "below and around it.",
  "And every",
  "raised house stood among",
  "streets and services",
  "that needed to connect",
  "at a new level.",
  "Water pipes,",
  "fire hydrants,",
  "and streetcar tracks",
  "also had to be",
  "dealt with",
  "as the level",
  "of the ground changed.",
  "This was",
  "not a model",
  "on an engineer's desk.",
  "It was a living",
  "city, full of structures",
  "that had",
  "to be kept",
  "in place",
  "while the land",
  "around them was remade.",
  "To bring in",
  "the material,",
  "a canal was cut",
  "through part of Galveston.",
  "Dredges collected",
  "sand",
  "and carried it",
  "through the canal.",
  "Workers then pumped",
  "fill into the areas",
  "being raised,",
  "including spaces",
  "beneath the lifted buildings.",
  "The amount varied",
  "from place to place.",
  "The aim",
  "was not to lift",
  "every street to exactly",
  "the same height,",
  "but to create",
  "a higher, sloping grade",
  "behind the seawall.",
  "What looked like",
  "chaos had a purpose:",
  "sand gradually",
  "became the new ground",
  "on which the city",
  "would stand.",
  "Once an area",
  "was filled",
  "to its new grade,",
  "foundations could be finished",
  "beneath the structures.",
  "Work could then move",
  "on to another section.",
  "The change was gradual,",
  "not a single",
  "dramatic lift",
  "of the entire island.",
  "Some residents continued",
  "living in their houses",
  "during the work.",
  "To get around,",
  "they used",
  "makeshift boardwalks raised",
  "above the muddy fill.",
  "Imagine stepping out",
  "of a front door",
  "onto a narrow",
  "wooden path",
  "while crews",
  "reshaped the ground below.",
  "The transformation also",
  "came at a cost.",
  "Taxpayers helped",
  "finance the work,",
  "and property owners",
  "had to pay",
  "for lifting their buildings.",
  "As streets and sidewalks",
  "disappeared beneath fill,",
  "residents faced the expense",
  "of replacing them too.",
  "The engineering solution",
  "was remarkable,",
  "but rebuilding placed real",
  "burdens on the people",
  "who remained.",
  "One of the most",
  "striking challenges",
  "was Saint Patrick's Church.",
  "The building",
  "weighed an estimated",
  "three thousand tons.",
  "According to the Galveston",
  "and Texas History Center,",
  "workers used seven hundred",
  "jacks to raise",
  "it five feet.",
  "A heavy masonry church,",
  "moved upward",
  "not by a single",
  "enormous machine,",
  "but by the patient",
  "coordination of many",
  "smaller lifts.",
  "The main work",
  "continued for years.",
  "Temporary supports",
  "disappeared beneath new foundations.",
  "The temporary canal",
  "was filled back in.",
  "Streets were rebuilt.",
  "Little by little,",
  "the strange city",
  "of boardwalks",
  "and raised houses",
  "gave way to a",
  "more familiar one.",
  "Then another hurricane",
  "put the defenses",
  "to the test.",
  "In 1915,",
  "a powerful storm",
  "struck the region.",
  "Galveston suffered damage,",
  "but the loss",
  "of life",
  "in the city",
  "was far",
  "lower than in 1900.",
  "The seawall",
  "and raised ground",
  "had become",
  "part of a broader",
  "response to a danger",
  "the city",
  "now understood much better.",
  "That did not make",
  "Galveston invulnerable.",
  "Hurricanes continued",
  "to threaten the island,",
  "and in 2008",
  "Hurricane Ike brought",
  "a major surge",
  "to the Texas coast.",
  "No wall",
  "can erase the sea",
  "or guarantee that every",
  "future storm",
  "will be survived",
  "without loss.",
  "But the people",
  "of Galveston",
  "had done something extraordinary.",
  "After a disaster",
  "that destroyed thousands",
  "of lives,",
  "they chose not only",
  "to rebuild their city.",
  "They changed",
  "the ground beneath it.",
  "For years,",
  "homes stood",
  "above muddy streets",
  "while workers",
  "brought in the sand",
  "that would make",
  "a different future possible.",
  "The storm had revealed",
  "how vulnerable Galveston was.",
  "The answer was written,",
  "piece by piece,",
  "into the shape",
  "of the city itself."
]
